    "https://ejgl.fa.ap1.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/UOW/job/7091": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Governance",
      "description": "Associate Director, Governance - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Associate Director, Governance Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW) - a purpose driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role As Associate Director, Governance , you will lead the development and continuous improvement of UOW’s institutional governance frameworks; driving best practice governance, policy oversight, delegations management and governance capability uplift across the institution. This is a substantive, institution-shaping role. You will ensure UOW’s governance architecture is aligned with legislative requirements, the Expert Council on University Governance (ECUG) principles and UOW’s Strategic Plan 2030, and that it keeps pace with the demands of a complex, evolving higher education environment. Working closely with the Associate Director, Secretariat, you will ensure governance frameworks and Council operations are coherent and effectively integrated — with a clear distinction between this role’s focus on governance architecture and framework, and the Secretariat’s focus on operational committee delivery. You will lead a dedicated team of governance professionals, provide expert advice to senior executives and Council, and build governance capability across faculties and divisions in an environment where accountability and continuous improvement genuinely matter. About the Team The Governance team supports the integrity, effectiveness and accountability of decision-making across the University. Partnering closely with senior leaders and stakeholders from across the institution, the team delivers expert advice, governance oversight and strategic support in an environment that is both complex and constantly evolving. As Associate Director, you will lead a highly capable team and have the opportunity to shape governance practices, drive continuous improvement and contribute to initiatives that have a genuine and lasting impact across the University. This is a role for someone who enjoys working at the intersection of strategy, governance and leadership, and who is motivated by the opportunity to influence meaningful organisational outcomes. What You’ll Bring You are a respected and influential leader with deep governance expertise and a passion for helping organisations perform at their best. You bring sound judgement, political acumen and the ability to provide trusted advice in complex environments where competing priorities, risk and strategic objectives intersect. You thrive on building strong relationships and have a proven ability to influence, collaborate and achieve outcomes through others. Combining strategic thinking with a practical and solutions-focused approach, you can translate governance principles into meaningful action that strengthens accountability, enables effective decision-making and supports organisational success. You will bring: Significant experience leading governance, policy, compliance, legal, risk or related functions within a complex organisation. Strong knowledge of contemporary governance frameworks, principles and best practice. Demonstrated success leading, developing and empowering high-performing teams. Exceptional stakeholder engagement and influencing skills, with the ability to establish credibility and build trusted relationships at all levels. Experience providing expert advice to senior executives, committees and decision-making bodies on complex and often sensitive matters. Strong analytical, communication and problem-solving capabilities, coupled with sound judgement and professional integrity. A commitment to continuous improvement and the ability to drive change that delivers sustainable organisational outcomes Why Join UOW 35-hour full-time work week supporting greater balance and flexibility Flexible working arrangements and family-friendly policies Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas–New Year period Purchased leave options to provide greater flexibility throughout the year Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Employment type: Full-time 5 year fixed-term appointment Salary: Level 10 | Competitive remuneration package + 12% superannuation Position Description Location: Wollongong Campus with hybrid work arrangements Work Rights: Valid Australian work rights required.  Visa sponsorship is not available. How to Apply Click on the ‘Apply Now’ button at the bottom of the advertisement. You’ll be requested to submit a CV, and cover letter (of no more than 3 pages) summarising your skills and experience as they relate to the selection criteria located in the position description. For further information about this position, please contact Erin Snape on + 61 2 4221 3273. Closing Date: Sunday 15 November 2026, 11:55pm Equity, Diversity & Inclusion The University of Wollongong is committed to fostering an inclusive and equitable workplace where diversity is valued, respected and celebrated.  We strive to create a workplace that reflects the communities we serve, removes barriers to participation, and provides equitable opportunities for staff to reach their full potential. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people of all gender identities and sexual orientations, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, people with disability, and those with caring or family responsibilities. As required by federal legislation, prospective employees are required to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender based Violence or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender based Violence, during their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. Any such declaration will be included in the University’s employment screening processes and will be treated with the strictest confidence and in compliance with all privacy legislation. About Us At the University of Wollongong (UOW) , our people are united by a shared purpose — to create a better future through education, research, innovation and meaningful community impact. With deep local roots and a growing global presence, UOW is proud to contribute to positive change in the communities we serve and the world beyond them. Guided by our Vision 2035 and Strategic Plan 2030 , we are building a future that is innovative, inclusive and committed to societal impact — one where people, ideas and opportunity can thrive. We are recognised for excellence in teaching and research, and for the real-world impact of our work. But what truly brings UOW to life is our people. Across every role, our staff contribute to something bigger — helping shape the future through the work they do every day. At UOW, we are committed to fostering a culture where people feel valued, supported and empowered to do their best work. Our Values in Action guide how we work, lead and make decisions — creating a workplace grounded in integrity, accountability, collaboration and excellence. Joining UOW means becoming part of a values-led community where your work has purpose, your contribution is valued, and the impact you make can be felt locally and globally. Apply Now Job Info Job Identification 7091 Job Category Legal & Compliance Posting Date 10/29/2026, 08:18 PM Apply Before 11/15/2026, 04:55 AM Job Schedule Full time Locations Northfields Ave, Wollongong, NSW, 2522, AU Similar Jobs Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies Contact Us Feedback Privacy Statement and Policies UOW Home Page Why work at UOW UOW Global Presence UOW in Dubai UOW in Hong Kong UOW in Malaysia Our People UOW Pulse I am an employee Are You Still With Us? It seems you've been gone for a while. For security reasons we will end your session automatically in 03:00 unless you would like to continue working. End Session Continue Working Work Summary This summary is generated by AI Assist. Click inside the summary text box to make changes as necessary. 1000 Required Discard Add Summary Page Associate Director, Governance - University of Wollongong Careers loaded"
