      "title": "Technical Officer",
      "description": "Technical Officer - Human Physiology - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Technical Officer - Human Physiology South Western Sydney, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW) - a purpose‑driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role We are seeking a Technical Officer to provide high-quality laboratory and technical support for Human Physiology teaching at the UOW Liverpool Campus. This hands-on role supports laboratory planning, practical class delivery, equipment maintenance, anatomy teaching resources, resource development and class set-up and pack-down to ensure a safe and engaging learning environment for students and staff. Key responsibilities: Support the delivery of Human Physiology practical laboratory teaching Prepare, maintain and calibrate laboratory equipment and teaching resources Support anatomy teaching resources and laboratory operations Manage laboratory inventories, procurement, maintenance and repairs Promote safe, compliant and efficient laboratory environments About the Team The School of Medical, Indigenous & Health Sciences offers courses in Exercise Science and Rehabilitation, Nutrition and Dietetics, Medical and Health Sciences and Health Sciences (Indigenous Studies). This structure provides opportunities for cross-disciplinary teaching and research. What You’ll Bring Qualifications or equivalent experience in Health, Medica Science, Exercise Science, Science or a related field Experience supporting laboratory operations, including the use, maintenance and calibration of physiology teaching equipment Knowledge of human physiology, anatomy and associated laboratory practices Sound understanding of laboratory safety, WHS requirements and safe work practices Strong organisational and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work independently and manage competing priorities Why Join 