      "title": "2 x Senior Business Analyst",
      "description": "2  x Senior Business Analyst - Cyber and IDAM - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs 2  x Senior Business Analyst - Cyber and IDAM Wollongong, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW) — a purpose‑driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. The University of Wollongong is undertaking a significant Cyber Security Uplift Program and is seeking experienced Senior Business Analysts to join our team. We have opportunities across two streams: Senior Business Analyst - Cyber Security Senior Business Analyst - Identity & Access Management (IDAM) These roles will play a key part in delivering strategic cyber security and identity initiatives that strengthen the University's security posture, improve governance and access controls, and support our broader digital transformation agenda. About the Roles Working closely with project managers, technical specialists, vendors, and business stakeholders, you will lead business analysis activities across complex cyber security projects. You will facilitate workshops, gather and document requirements, map business processes, support solution design, and ensure solutions meet business and security objectives. Depending on your area of expertise, you may contribute to initiatives involving: Cyber Security Cyber security control uplift and assurance activities Security assessments and remediation programs Process improvement aligned with frameworks such as NIST, ISO 27001 and Essential Eight Security solution implementation and testing Business readiness and stakeholder engagement activities Identity & Access Management (IDAM) Privileged Access Management (PAM) Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) User Access Certification (UAC) Single Sign-On (SSO) and Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) Identity governance and access management process improvement initiatives What You’ll Bring You are an experienced Business Analyst who enjoys working at the intersection of business and technology. You have strong stakeholder engagement skills and can confidently translate complex technical concepts into practical business outcomes. To be successful, you will bring: Extensive experience as a Business Analyst delivering cyber security, identity, access management or other enterprise technology projects Strong requirements gathering, business process analysis and process redesign skills Experience facilitating workshops and engaging diverse stakeholder groups Experience supporting testing, implementation and change activities The ability to work effectively with technical teams, business leaders and external vendors Tertiary qualifications in Business, Information Technology or a related discipline, or equivalent experience Why Join UOW Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation 35-hour full-time work week supporting greater balance and flexibility Flexible working arrangements and family-friendly policies Generous leave entitlements including additional concession days over the Christmas–New Year period Ongoing professional development and clear career progression opportunities Role Details Both roles are Fixed-term, Full-time appointments with an end date of December 2027 Level 8/9: $123,283 - $152,959 plus superannuation. Salary is commensurate with experience and capability. Location: Campus / Hybrid working Valid Australian work rights required. Visa sponsorship is not available The successful candidate will be required to provide a valid Criminal History Check prior to commencement. Position Description Senior Business Analyst Cyber Security Position Description Senior Business Analyst IDAM How to Apply Click on the ‘Apply Now’ button at the bottom of the advertisement. You’ll be requested to submit a resume, and cover letter (of no more than 3 pages) summarising your skills and experience as they relate to the selection criteria located in the position descrip