      "description": "Lecturer in Medical Sciences - Human Physiology and Pathophysiology - University of Wollongong Careers Skip to main content. sitemap Profile Sign Out View More Jobs Lecturer in Medical Sciences - Human Physiology and Pathophysiology South Western Sydney, NSW, Australia Job Description Make an impact at the University of Wollongong (UOW) - a purpose‑driven institution ranked in the top 1% of universities globally. About the Role Bring your expertise in Medical Sciences to our Liverpool campus, delivering engaging industry-informed teaching across areas including human physiology and pathophysiology. You'll contribute to curriculum development, teaching hands on practical laboratories in our brand-new Liverpool campus, student supervision and the ongoing enhancement of our programs while building your research profile and supporting the broader activities of the School. The appointee will collaborate closely with colleagues at the Wollongong campus to ensure innovative, sustainable and aligned teaching approaches and collaboration across both locations. Key responsibilities: Deliver high-quality teaching and learning experiences Help shape future-focused Medical Sciences programs Support student success and development Contribute to research and scholarly activity Build meaningful external partnerships Contribute to a vibrant academic community About the Team The School of Medical, Indigenous and Health Sciences (MIHS) includes disciplines of Medical Sciences; Nutrition Science and Dietetics; Indigenous Health; Occupational Health and Safety; Public Heath; and Exercise, Sport and Rehabilitation Sciences. The School currently offers externally accredited programs in Dietetics, Clinical Exercise Physiology and Exercise Science, Occupational Health and Safety, as well as non-accredited programs in Medical and Health Sciences, Pre-Medicine, Public Health, Nutrition Sciences, Indigenous Trauma and Recovery Practice, and Indigenous Health. What You’ll 